"Plugin API" means the interface that RazorFX offers to plugins, as defined in the file
razorfx/plugin_api.py and documented in docs/PLUGIN_API.md in the same version of
RazorFX. It consists of: the public names of that module (names that do not start with
an underscore) and their documented behaviour; the plugin.json manifest format; the
plugin directories RazorFX searches; the register(ctx) and unregister() entry points; and
the objects and data RazorFX passes to a plugin through them, to the extent they are
documented there.

"Independent Plugin" means a work that
  (a) is loaded and run by RazorFX's plugin loader,
  (b) interacts with RazorFX only through the Plugin API, and
  (c) is not based on RazorFX: it contains no part of RazorFX other than what section 2(a)
      allows, and it is not a modified version of RazorFX.
Using the names, signatures, constants and data formats of the Plugin API, to the extent
needed to interoperate with it, does not by itself make a work based on RazorFX. An
Independent Plugin may also use other libraries (including Qt for Python / PySide6)
directly, as long as it reaches RazorFX itself only through the Plugin API.

"Combined Work" means RazorFX running together with one or more Independent Plugins, for
example in the same process.


